{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Let the earth bring forth a living soul.</b> Our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted this as referring to the spirit of the first man; and he says: this refers to the bestial soul in man, which has no portion with the supernal beings, but returns to the dust immediately upon the death of the body, like the spirit of the beast, concerning which it is written (Ecclesiastes 3:21): ״ורוח הבהמה היורדת היא למטה לארץ״; or the intention is concerning the soul of wisdom, and the meaning of 'the earth' mentioned in the first verse is the land of the living." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״תוצא הארץ נפש חיה״ — it is written 'in souls'; ״ויעש אלהים את חית הארץ למינה ואת הבהמה״ etc. — it is written 'in bodies.' And the explanation of the matter: 'it is written in souls' — this is the living soul of beast and creeping thing and beast of the earth; and what it says, 'it is written in bodies,' is because it did not mention 'living soul' as it had mentioned in the command." "<b>And further.</b> By way of the Midrash, Bereshit Rabbah: ״ויעש אלהים את חית הארץ״ — Rabbi Hoshaya Rabbah says: this is the serpent. Rabbi says: ״נפש חיה״ — these are the מריאים; the Holy One, blessed be He, created their souls, and when He came to create their bodies, He sanctified the day and did not create them, to teach you proper conduct: that if a person has a fine article or a fine pearl in his possession on the eve of Sabbath, they say to him: cast it from your hand, 'it is enough for the servant to be as his master.' The meaning of מריאים: demons."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:27:23.597232694Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}